<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Autonomous Albanian Republic of Korçë</h1><p class="st-meta">1916 CE – 1920 CE · capital Korçë</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Albanian autonomous region set up under French military protection during the First World War, which gave Korçë its own schools, money and stamps.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> French forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-front">Salonika front</a> occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korce">Korçë</a> in late 1916. To secure the area against Greek irregulars and win local support, the French commander signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protocol-of-korce">Protocol of Korçë</a> in December 1916 with Albanian notables, creating an autonomous Albanian province under French protection, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/themistokli-germenji">Themistokli Gërmenji</a> as prefect of police.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A council of Christian and Muslim Albanian representatives ran the town and surrounding villages, and Albanian became the language of administration and schools, including the first Albanian secular secondary school. The republic issued its own stamps and banknotes and flew an Albanian flag with French colours. Real authority lay with the French army.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> ended the autonomy in February 1918 and governed the district militarily, Gërmenji having been executed by a French court in 1917. In 1920 French troops withdrew and handed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korce">Korçë</a> to the Albanian government created at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushnje">Lushnjë</a>, ensuring it stayed in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> rather than <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/autonomous-albanian-republic-of-korce.jpg" alt="Autonomous Albanian Republic of Korçë" width="320" height="229"><figcaption>Image: Auteur inconnu; derivative work by Titimaster · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Koritsa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1916 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Korçë</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Themistokli Gërmenji</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity, Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Korçë</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=autonomous-albanian-republic-of-korce" aria-label="Autonomous Albanian Republic of Korçë on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5189 727 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Autonomous Albanian Republic of Korçë lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5509 983L5054 728M5509 983L5475 960"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5475 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5509 983h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5509 983h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Korçë. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=autonomous-albanian-republic-of-korce">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
